A||N||16||Elenor84||Just put in an excel super coil and it runs worse then ever...||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||07-12-2001||01:46 PM||||Hey guys...I just completly redid my ignition system and a few other minor things in the engine.  I put in a new cap and rotor, Excel 8.8 wires, Bosh platinum Plugs and Excel Super Coil...now the coil that I got had 2 connecting ends for it...both of them didn't work...so I took the GM side and spliced all the wires and crimpt ends onto them and put it in the original harness.  Now, my car did start...but wen I went to go ajust the wire from the distributer to the coil I got a big shock!  Kinda hurt but I'm alright...I saw dead people for a minute or two...anyways...why did I get shocked and why now is my car taking longer to start and idle's ruffer?  Thx guys!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-12-2001||02:15 PM||||are you sure u didnt cross the two wires when you spliced em? that shock is called 40,000+ volts. did you put the new plug wires in the correct firing order?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||07-12-2001||02:26 PM||||yes the plug wires are in correct firing order or else they wouldn't fire...and no I didn't mix the two wires up because I fliped them around(the grounds...not the actual positive and negitive wires, I"m not that stupid)and then my car wouldn't start...so I put them back and it did...it just doesen't start as smooth...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||07-12-2001||03:50 PM||||Just an FYI -- Volts Hurts -- AMPS KILL!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||07-12-2001||03:56 PM||||Is this for a 4 or 6cyl? A 6cyl can start with mixup wires. The shock is voltage jumping from the ignition to you. Were you barefoot? Put rubber shoes. I do have had couple of those shocks.<BR>I know details for coils in 6cyl but not for 4cyl.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Elenor84||07-12-2001||04:42 PM||||Ya its for a 4 cylinder...u know...now that I think about it I think I was barefoot...I don't mind that it shocked me I just don't want it to happen everytime I touch my engine while its runnin...I have an 84 4 cylinder witch I hear has no connector...I think I pulled it off pritty good but why is it running so ruff?  What can I do now to change it?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||07-12-2001||04:48 PM||||You got shocked because your wires are leaking. With wires that are leaking electricity your car will misfire under load and generally run like crap.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Elenor84||07-12-2001||06:01 PM||||How do I fix these so called leaking wires?<BR>Electrical tape?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||StuGood||07-12-2001||06:20 PM||||Electrical tape is a temporary fix, for when you know where it's leaking and you need it to get by.<P>Preferred (permanent) fix is set of new plug wires.  I get mine at ("Koolwire") Pep Boys - reasonably priced and seem to be very reliable, for me.  More expensive doesn't necessarily mean better, it seems, but careful installation (routing) is the key.  So thinks me, anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Elenor84||07-12-2001||06:24 PM||||but I just bought new spark plug wires...Excel 8.8s<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||DRH||07-12-2001||06:31 PM||||Didn't you say you put new plug wires on? They shouldn't be "leaking". <P>Is it running rough like one cylinder not firing part (or all) of the time? Double check all your plug wire connections. Also, double check the cap and rotor are on correctly. If you have a bad connection (like a wire with the boot on the plug or cap, but the wire not) this will make it more likely to get a shock from the coil wire. If it can't get to the plug, it'll go the best available route, which could be your hand.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||DRH||07-12-2001||06:33 PM||||Oops, you posted while I was typing. It does have new wire.<P>Also, did you check the gap on the plugs?||||reg||1
Z||000012||bHooper||07-12-2001||06:35 PM||||also, make sure you have a new control module... or it will fry the first time out.<P>mine did, last winter.  fortunatly i was only a half mile from Bob Englert's house when it happened!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jncomutt||07-13-2001||12:50 AM||||BHooper, you mean it needs to be replaced because he changed the coil??  Just changed my coil to a MSD Blaster GM, am I awaiting a bad control module. (I'm gettin 6A anyway next week) Or, Did I miss something and am totally off topic???||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||07-13-2001||08:08 AM|||| [QUOTE]Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR>[b]yes the plug wires are in correct firing order or else they wouldn't fire...and no I didn't mix the two wires up because I fliped them around(the grounds...not the actual positive and negitive wires, I"m not that stupid)and then my car wouldn't start...so I put them back and it did...it just doesen't start as smooth...<BR>[quote]<P><BR>I put a new coil in my Mercedes and somehow I got the gnd and pos wires switched. It still ran and started fine, just cut out and missed at higher rpm (ya I was stupid, but s**t happens). Me and 3 garages could not find out why the miss till we put a scope on the engine and found only about 7,000 volts were passing thru plug wires. A lot of people I know just intall new plugs and dont check the gaps before. As a last resort, the new coil may be bad. New doesnt mean it works. You can stick it on another car and see if it still messes up.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula88||07-13-2001||09:14 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>Hey guys...I just completly redid my ignition system and a few other minor things in the engine.  I put in a new cap and rotor, Excel 8.8 wires, Bosh platinum Plugs and Excel Super Coil</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, there's your problem. You're using <B>Excel</B> parts.  Microsoft never was very good in the automotive parts division.  I've heard people have gotten better results with Accel ignition parts.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>But I've also heard of problems with them.  I would stick with AC Delco, or go with MSD if I was going aftermarket.  <p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000016||bHooper||07-13-2001||09:50 AM||||hahahaha... the fiero nerd made a computer nerd joke!  just kidding, john... i am really only jealouse (accept for the fiero thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
